<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wars of the Three Kingdoms</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1639">1639</a>–<a href="/years/1653">1653</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as British Civil Wars</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Wars of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-kingdoms-period">Three Kingdoms</a> were a series of linked wars from 1639 to 1653 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and Ireland, then ruled by Charles I. They included the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishops-wars">Bishops' Wars</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irish-confederate-wars">Irish Confederate Wars</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-civil-war">English Civil War</a>, fought over religion, royal power and the relations between the three kingdoms. They ended with the execution of Charles I and the conquest of Scotland and Ireland by the Commonwealth.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-three-kingdoms.jpg" alt="Wars of the Three Kingdoms" width="320" height="268" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sir Anthony Van Dyck (1599 - 1641) Details on Google Art Project · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_Anthony_Van_Dyck_-_Charles_I_(1600-49)_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
